NOTE FOR THE PROJECT OWNER

This is a deliberately plain statement of intent, not a standard licence, and it
has not been reviewed by a lawyer. The collector under /collector is MIT on
purpose -- it runs on other people's servers and must be readable and freely
usable, or nobody will install it. The backend is what a hosted service would be
sold as, so it should not be MIT.

Before publishing, replace this file with the official text of whichever
standard form you choose. The usual choices for exactly this situation are:

  - Business Source License 1.1 (converts to an open licence after a set period)
  - Elastic License 2.0 (shorter; forbids offering the software as a service)

Both are published texts that should be copied verbatim rather than paraphrased.
